= Discussion
// Every branch below was written before the data existed. Exactly one
// renders; which one is decided by the experiment, not the author.
#if dir == "cooling" [
  The observed decline is consistent with passive heat loss to the room: the
  sample began above ambient and relaxed toward it, as Newton's law predicts
  for a well-mixed body with surface-limited exchange. The practical
  implication in our pre-registration applies: samples prepared warm must be
  used within roughly one time constant if their temperature matters.
] else if dir == "heating" [
  A temperature *rise* was pre-registered as evidence that the sample started
  below ambient, or that an unaccounted heat source (stirring, exothermic
  contamination, direct sunlight) dominated passive exchange. The apparatus
  should be inspected before any physical interpretation is attempted.
] else [
  The change in temperature did not exceed three times the residual noise, so
  under the pre-registered rule we treat the sample as thermally constant
  over the observation window. This outcome was anticipated for samples
  prepared near ambient; a longer window or a larger initial offset would be
  required to detect exchange.
]

#if R.conclusive [
  Because the effect cleared the pre-registered threshold
  (|#f(R.delta)| #sym.gt 3 #sym.times #f(R.noise_c, d: 2)), we regard the
  direction stated above as the finding of this experiment.
] else [
  Because the effect did not clear the pre-registered threshold, this report
  makes *no* directional claim; by design, the wording above cannot overstate
  the evidence.
]

= Reproducibility
`just all` verifies the pinned data hash, reruns the analysis, and recompiles
this PDF and the summary. Editing prose recompiles instantly in the live
preview; editing `scripts/analysis.py` or `data/` regenerates every value on
this page. The build history, comments, and signed checkpoints travel with
the project's git repository.
